OpenChamber Agent Browser 1.0.0 (local adaptation)

The browser-provider, surface, panel, and browser-runtime source in this local
package is adapted from Server Browser v0.7.0, upstream commit
6c5e76ddfa21b574d0521a27f408cd643673161c:
https://github.com/JosueGalRe/openchamber-server-browser/tree/6c5e76ddfa21b574d0521a27f408cd643673161c
Copyright (c) 2025 Bohdan Triapitsyn. The upstream project is MIT licensed;
see LICENSE. This package is a separate local 1.0.0 adaptation, not an
upstream Server Browser release. It changes the upstream per-chat
manager to one shared browser owner and adds the MCP broker, loopback relay,
and the policy/runtime changes in this package.

The upstream Server Browser v0.7.0 README describes that project's browser
backend as an extraction of OpenChamber PR #3425, with source reference commit
362dbc3f305615200d762b721106c64e796b095b:
https://github.com/JosueGalRe/openchamber/tree/362dbc3f305615200d762b721106c64e796b095b
Copyright (c) 2025 Bohdan Triapitsyn. This is the inherited source reference
identified by upstream; it is distinct from the Server Browser v0.7.0 commit
used as the direct adaptation baseline.

The extension targets @openchamber/sdk 2.1.1 from the npm registry, as pinned
in package.json and bun.lock. The service bundle includes @openchamber/sdk,
zod, and ws under their MIT licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

The 37 browser tool names and input-schema contract are parity-checked against
the running Obscura v0.2.4 tools/list capture supplied for this integration.
The browser tool implementations in this package are local code; no Obscura
implementation is vendored.
